#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:17
msgid "Get Started with Bluetooth"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:19
msgid "The ESPC2-01 gives you **Wi-Fi and Bluetooth in the same module**, so the kit needs no second Bluetooth chip. The Bluetooth projects use exactly the module you already have."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:22
msgid "In the Wi-Fi projects the board talked to Blynk through the cloud. Here the phone talks to the module **directly** - no router, no internet, no account. That is what makes Bluetooth so useful for a remote control or a small display."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:26
msgid "By the end of this chapter you will have:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:28
msgid "The module advertising itself as **SunFounder-C2**,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:29
msgid "Text typed on the phone arriving on the board, and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:30
msgid "Text typed on the board appearing on the phone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:34
msgid "1. Connect the Module"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:36
msgid "Wire the module to the R4 Minima the same way as in the Wi-Fi projects: **5V, GND, TX, RX** - four wires, nothing else."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:41
msgid "The module draws a high current at start-up, so make sure the 9 V battery or an external power supply is plugged into the DC jack of the R4 Minima."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:50
msgid "2. Upload the Sketch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:52
msgid "Open ``00-Bluetooth_start.ino`` under the path of ``ultimate-sensor-kit\\code\\iot_project_espc201\\bluetooth\\00-Bluetooth_start``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:54
msgid "Select **Arduino UNO R4 Minima** and the right port, then click **Upload**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:56
msgid "The sketch does three things:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:58
msgid "It includes ``SunFounder_BLE.h``, a small wrapper around the module's Bluetooth commands - this is why the rest of the code only needs ``bleSerial.print()`` and ``bleSerial.read()``;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:61
msgid "At start-up the wrapper switches Bluetooth on, sets the name to **SunFounder-C2** and starts advertising, so a phone can find it;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:63
msgid "After that the sketch simply passes text in both directions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:71
msgid "Open the Serial Monitor at **115200**. You should read:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:83
msgid "If you read ``[!] no reply from the module`` instead, the module is not answering on D0/D1 - check the four wires and the power supply, then press the reset button on the board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:89
msgid "3. Find the Module with Your Phone"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:91
msgid "Install **LightBlue** on your phone - it is free on iOS and Android. Any Bluetooth scanner works, but the screens below use LightBlue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:100
msgid "Open LightBlue and tap **Scan**. The module appears as **SunFounder-C2**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:104
msgid "The name comes from the sketch. If you change it there, the new name is what appears on the phone - handy when several kits are in the same room."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:109
msgid "**Do not pair the module in the Bluetooth settings of the phone.** This is BLE, so there is nothing to pair: LightBlue opens the connection itself. If you tap **SunFounder-C2** under *Settings > Bluetooth*, Android or iOS starts the older pairing procedure and asks for a PIN code - and the module has no code to give, so the box can never be filled in correctly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:115
msgid "If you already tried: open *Settings > Bluetooth*, choose **Forget this device** (or *Unpair*), switch Bluetooth off and on again, then connect from LightBlue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:124
msgid "Tap **SunFounder-C2** to connect. The service list opens."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:126
msgid "Expand the service **0xA002**. It holds the characteristics **C300** to **C307**. The three used in this chapter are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:133
msgid "Characteristic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:134
msgid "Direction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:135
msgid "What it is for"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:136
msgid "**C304**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:137
msgid "phone -> board"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:138
msgid "the phone writes text here and the board reads it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:139
msgid "**C305**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:140
#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:143
msgid "board -> phone"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:141
msgid "the board pushes text here; the phone has to **Subscribe** first"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:142
msgid "**C300**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:144
msgid "one stored value the phone can **Read** at any time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:153
msgid "4. Send Text from the Phone to the Board"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:155
msgid "Open **0xC304** and tap **Write new value**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:163
msgid "Change the format - the button in the top right corner - to **UTF-8 String**, then type a word, for example ``hello``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:168
msgid "This step is easy to forget. In the default hex format the board receives the numbers ``68 65 6C 6C 6F`` instead of the word ``hello``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:177
msgid "Look at the Serial Monitor: your text appears there, and the board sends it straight back so you can see that the link works both ways."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:187
msgid "5. Send Text from the Board to the Phone"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:189
msgid "Open **0xC305** and tap **Subscribe**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:191
msgid "**Subscribe** means \"keep this open and show me everything that arrives\". Without it the phone silently drops anything the board sends."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:200
msgid "In the Serial Monitor, type a word and press **Enter**. The sketch forwards it to C305, so it shows up in LightBlue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:209
msgid "If you see hex numbers in LightBlue instead of your text, set the format in the top right corner to **UTF-8 String** - the same setting as in step 4."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:219
msgid "6. What You Just Learned"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:221
msgid "**Write** (C304) - the phone sends data to the board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:222
msgid "**Subscribe** (C305) - the board sends data to the phone, and the phone listens."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:223
msgid "**Read** (C300) - the phone asks for a value whenever it likes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/00-iot_bluetooth_start.rst:225
msgid "The next chapters use exactly these three, only the text and the hardware change: an LCD that shows what you type, a lock that opens, an RGB lamp that changes colour."
msgstr ""
